# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendor artefacts — never commit these.
#
# The CareLink uploader is proprietary Medtronic software. Its JARs and the
# installer are not ours to redistribute, and they carry material that must not
# enter a public repo:
#
#   * `uploader.jks` / `uploader.policy` — keystore and security policy
#   * `uploader.cfg`, `localweb/*.json` — runtime configuration, some of which
#     carries base64 key material (`sakeKey`, `secureToken`) even when shipped
#     as templates
#   * `CareLinkUploader-install.txt` — the install log, which records the
#     operator's macOS account name in `su <user> -c ...` lines. That is a
#     personal identifier and must never be committed.
#   * any `.dmg`, `.app` bundle, or extracted `.dat` payload
#
# Findings about these artefacts are published in findings-log/ as prose and
# derived numbers. The artefacts themselves stay local.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.dmg
*.jar
*.jks
*.app/
*.dat
App/
Extracted/
mac-copy/
uploader.log
CareLinkUploader-install.txt
localweb/
*.pkcs12
*.p12
*.keystore
